{
  "title": "Le {ip:telefono}: {ip:voglio} aiutarla",
  "translation": "I'm phoning her: I want to help her",
  "topics": "Direct and indirect object pronouns, pronouns with infinitives and modal verbs",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      {
        "h": "Direct or indirect?"
      },
      "Look at the question the verb answers. *Whom? What?* needs a direct pronoun: *{ip:Conosco} Luca → Lo {ip:conosco}*. *To whom?*, with the preposition *a* in front of the person, needs an indirect one: *{ip:Telefono} a Luca → Gli {ip:telefono}*.",
      "The two sets are identical except in the third person, so that is the only part you have to learn.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Direct: whom?",
            "Indirect: to whom?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "me",
              "mi",
              "mi"
            ],
            [
              "you",
              "ti",
              "ti"
            ],
            [
              "him",
              "**lo**",
              "**gli**"
            ],
            [
              "her",
              "**la**",
              "**le**"
            ],
            [
              "us",
              "ci",
              "ci"
            ],
            [
              "you (plural)",
              "vi",
              "vi"
            ],
            [
              "them (masc.)",
              "**li**",
              "**gli**"
            ],
            [
              "them (fem.)",
              "**le**",
              "**gli**"
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      "Common verbs with an indirect person: *telefonare a, parlare a, scrivere a, dire a, dare a, regalare a, chiedere a, rispondere a*.",
      {
        "h": "Where the pronoun goes"
      },
      "It normally stands right before the verb: *Le {ip:telefono} stasera. Non lo {ip:conosco}.*",
      "With an infinitive, it attaches to the end, and the infinitive loses its final *-e*: *comprare + lo → comprarlo*.",
      "With *potere, volere* and *dovere* you may choose: the two versions mean exactly the same.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Before the modal",
            "After the infinitive"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "**Lo** {ip:voglio} comprare.",
              "{ip:Voglio} comprar**lo**."
            ],
            [
              "**Ti** {ip:posso} aiutare.",
              "{ip:Posso} aiutar**ti**."
            ],
            [
              "**Gli** {ip:devo} telefonare.",
              "{ip:Devo} telefonar**gli**."
            ]
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "h": "In the passato prossimo"
      },
      "Direct pronouns *lo, la, li, le* make the participle agree with them, as if it were an adjective. *Lo* and *la* become *l'* before the auxiliary. Indirect pronouns change nothing.",
      {
        "table": {
          "head": [
            "Pronoun",
            "Example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "lo",
              "L'{pp:ho vist**o**}."
            ],
            [
              "la",
              "L'{pp:ho vist**a**}."
            ],
            [
              "li",
              "Li {pp:ho vist**i**}."
            ],
            [
              "le",
              "Le {pp:ho vist**e**}."
            ],
            [
              "gli / le (indirect)",
              "Le {pp:ho telefonato}."
            ]
          ]
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "use": {
    "exercises": [
      {
        "type": "choice",
        "prompt": "Choose the right pronoun.",
        "questions": [
          {
            "q": "{ip:Conosco} Marco. ___ {ip:conosco}.",
            "options": [
              "*Lo",
              "Gli"
            ]
          },
          {
            "q": "{ip:Telefono} a Marco. ___ {ip:telefono}.",
            "options": [
              "Lo",
              "*Gli"
            ]
          },
          {
            "q": "{ip:Telefono} ad Anna. ___ {ip:telefono}.",
            "options": [
              "La",
              "*Le"
            ]
          },
          {
            "q": "{ip:Vedo} Anna. ___ {ip:vedo}.",
            "options": [
              "*La",
              "Le"
            ]
          },
          {
            "q": "{ip:Scrivo} ai miei amici. ___ {ip:scrivo}.",
            "options": [
              "Li",
              "*Gli"
            ]
          },
          {
            "q": "{ip:Compro} le mele. ___ {ip:compro}.",
            "options": [
              "*Le",
              "Gli"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "gap",
        "prompt": "Rewrite with the pronoun attached to the infinitive.",
        "questions": [
          "Lo {ip:voglio} comprare. → {ip:Voglio} [[comprarlo]].",
          "Ti {ip:posso} aiutare. → {ip:Posso} [[aiutarti]].",
          "Le {ip:devo} telefonare. → {ip:Devo} [[telefonarle]].",
          "La {ip:vogliamo} invitare. → {ip:Vogliamo} [[invitarla]]."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "gap",
        "prompt": "Complete the participle.",
        "questions": [
          "{pp:Hai visto} Anna? Sì, l'{pp:ho} [[vista#pp]].",
          "{pp:Hai comprato} il pane? Sì, l'{pp:ho} [[comprato#pp]].",
          "{pp:Hai preso} le chiavi? Sì, le {pp:ho} [[prese#pp]].",
          "{pp:Hai letto} i libri? Sì, li {pp:ho} [[letti#pp]].",
          "{pp:Hai telefonato} a Sara? Sì, le {pp:ho} [[telefonato#pp]]."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
